      "nsfwLevel": 7,
      "description": "<p><strong>RA-Mix V2.0</strong></p><p>V2.0 is more of a refinement of RA-Mix than a complete overhaul.</p><p>One of the main changes was bringing some of the more realistic and 2.5D influence back into the merge. V1 leaned a little heavier toward the anime side than I originally intended, so I wanted V2 to have a wider stylistic range while still keeping the overall look and character of RA-Mix.</p><p>I also spent some time adjusting the merge layers to improve stability. With V1, I would occasionally run into structural issues during generation, so part of this update was focused on cleaning that up and making the model a little more consistent.</p><p>Lighting and depth also seem to have improved with the changes, particularly when pushing the model toward more detailed or less strictly anime-style images.</p><p>Overall, V2 isn't meant to be a massive change from V1. The goal was mostly to give RA-Mix a little more stylistic flexibility, bring back some of its realistic and 2.5D range, and improve the stability of the merge without losing what I liked about the original.</p>",
